[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3508487508","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112477#issuecomment-3508487508","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112477","id":3508487508,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7RH0VU","user":{"login":"naturally-intelligent","id":6783606,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODM2MDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6783606?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent","html_url":"https://github.com/naturally-intelligent","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-09T16:09:37Z","updated_at":"2025-11-09T16:27:14Z","body":"I can confirm this. In fact this issue was driving me nuts for a while trying many solutions including call_deferred but nothing makes it go away. And the error can be quite spammy.\n\nHowever for me, the order of the AudioStreamPlayer2D and the Enabler2D doesn't matter. Just having both in a scene causes an error. Deleting either one makes the error go away. \n\nI am using inherited scenes tho, so that might make a difference. In my parent scene I have an Enabler, and child scenes have Audio players. So the order might not be relevant because of that.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3508487508/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3513268626","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112477#issuecomment-3513268626","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112477","id":3513268626,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7RaDmS","user":{"login":"naturally-intelligent","id":6783606,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODM2MDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6783606?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent","html_url":"https://github.com/naturally-intelligent","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-10T18:17:41Z","updated_at":"2025-11-26T18:17:54Z","body":"Maybe we could have an option that surpresses this error from printing?\n\nIt's just clogging up my output with like 100+ errors w/backtraces every run\n\nEdit: there is a way, turn off std_err in Project Settings! This only stops from printing to the console, but the editor output still show them.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3513268626/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3750932700","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112477#issuecomment-3750932700","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112477","id":3750932700,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7fkrDc","user":{"login":"sigmund68k","id":9064423,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNjQ0MjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9064423?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k","html_url":"https://github.com/sigmund68k","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-14T18:09:10Z","updated_at":"2026-01-14T18:09:10Z","body":"I've tracked this down to where the issue happens, but I'm not sure what the correct behavior should be. \n\nWhen adding the test scene in question (with a VisibilityEnabler2D node followed by an AudioStreamHandler2D node, or a derived class that adds an AudioStreamHandler2D, or a child scene that contains an AudioStreamHandler2D) to the scene tree via add_child(), the following sequence happens:\n\n1.  add_child is invoked, calling _add_child_nocheck.\n2. The tree relationship is setup, and NOTIFICATION_ENTER_TREE is propagated through children.\n3. VisibileOnScreenEnabler2D handles this in \"_notification\" here:  \nvoid VisibleOnScreenEnabler2D::_notification(int p_what) {\n\tswitch (p_what) {\n\t\tcase NOTIFICATION_ENTER_TREE: {\n\t\t\tif (Engine::get_singleton()->is_editor_hint()) {\n\t\t\t\treturn;\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tnode_id = ObjectID();\n\t\t\tif (enable_node_path.is_empty()) {\n\t\t\t\treturn;\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\tNode *node = get_node(enable_node_path);\n\t\t\tif (node) {\n\t\t\t\tnode_id = node->get_instance_id();\n\t\t\t\tnode->set_process_mode(PROCESS_MODE_DISABLED);\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t} break;\n\n4. With an enable_node_path of \"..\", set_process_mode(PROCESS_MODE_DISABLED) is called on the parent node.\n5. This is processed in Node::set_rocess_mode (node.cpp:708), and results in the following booleans:\nprev_can_process = true, and prev_enabled = true (the VisibleOnScreenEnabler2D)\nnext_can_process = false, and next_enabled = false (the AudioStreamHandler2D)\nThis results in pause_notification = 14, and enabled_notification = 28\n\n(So, it's expected that the next node will be disabled and unable to process.)\n\n6. This gets forwarded / propagated down to the AudioStreamPlayer2D into AudioStreamPlayerInternal::notification:  \nvoid AudioStreamPlayerInternal::notification(int p_what) {\n\tswitch (p_what) {\n\n                <OTHER CASES DELETED>\n\n\t\tcase Node::NOTIFICATION_SUSPENDED:\n\t\tcase Node::NOTIFICATION_PAUSED: {\n\t\t\tif (!node->can_process()) {\n\t\t\t\t// Node can't process so we start fading out to silence\n\t\t\t\tset_stream_paused(true);\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t} break;\n\n                <OTHER CASES DELETED>\n\t}\n}\n\n7. \"if (!node->can_process())\" at audio_stream_player_internal.cpp:117 calls into Node::can_process:\n\tERR_FAIL_COND_V(!is_inside_tree(), false);\n\nThis notification is propagated to the AudioStreamHandler2D before it was added to the tree, resulting in this fail condition.\n\nQuestions:\n1. Should a can_process() call on a node that hasn't been added to the tree ALWAYS result in an ERR_FAIL_COND_V?\n2. Should the AudioStreamPlayer2D actually check !node->can_process()?  Is it safe to set_stream_paused if it's not on the tree yet?\n3. Should the AudioStreamPlayer2D do something else with this notification if it's not on the tree yet?\n\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3750932700/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3750941892","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112477#issuecomment-3750941892","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112477","id":3750941892,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7fktTE","user":{"login":"sigmund68k","id":9064423,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNjQ0MjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9064423?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k","html_url":"https://github.com/sigmund68k","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-14T18:11:25Z","updated_at":"2026-01-14T18:11:25Z","body":"<img width=\"1213\" height=\"818\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4cef8c10-7a2e-40db-acb9-f0c3d175c142\" />\n\nCall stack from VS.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3750941892/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3751667806","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112477#issuecomment-3751667806","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112477","id":3751667806,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7fnehe","user":{"login":"sigmund68k","id":9064423,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNjQ0MjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9064423?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k","html_url":"https://github.com/sigmund68k","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-14T20:51:59Z","updated_at":"2026-01-14T20:51:59Z","body":"I've got a simple fix that I'm going to propose for this, and submit as a PR.  \n\nAssumptions:\n * Calling can_process() on a node that is not on the tree is an error, and should be caught.  We should not change that behavior.\n * The AudioStreamPlayer2D should be actively aware of its presence on the tree, or not, and only use can_process() for its intended purpose if it believes it's actually on the tree.\n\nProposed fix:\n * In the notification handler for AudioStreamPlayer2D, explicitly check if the node is on the tree as part of a local \"can_process\" state, before calling the engine.\n\nI have this working now.  Working out the details to submit as a PR.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3751667806/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3751681809","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112477#issuecomment-3751681809","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112477","id":3751681809,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7fnh8R","user":{"login":"naturally-intelligent","id":6783606,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODM2MDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6783606?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent","html_url":"https://github.com/naturally-intelligent","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-14T20:56:15Z","updated_at":"2026-01-14T20:56:15Z","body":"Great work!! After reading your investigations I thought the same thing, checking if inside tree before checking can_process...\n\nHopefully that doesn't cause some unexpected behaviour or is against protocol","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3751681809/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3751788179","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112477#issuecomment-3751788179","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112477","id":3751788179,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7fn76T","user":{"login":"sigmund68k","id":9064423,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNjQ0MjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9064423?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k","html_url":"https://github.com/sigmund68k","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmu